## 1. Project Understanding & Architecture

### Exact Purpose of the Project
A retro-themed, highly responsive web-based **Snake Game** that allows users to play as guests or log in using Google OAuth to preserve their score history, track their personal best, and rank on a global Top 3 players leaderboard.

### Complete Architecture Diagram & Flow
The application follows a classic **client-server decoupled architecture (SPA + REST API)**.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Client [React SPA Frontend]
        App[App.jsx] --> AuthProvider[AuthContext.jsx]
        App --> Game[Game.jsx]
        App --> Leaderboard[Leaderboard.jsx]
        App --> Login[Login.jsx]
        Game --> gameLogic[gameLogic.js]
        Game --> API[api.js Interceptor]
    end

    subgraph Transport [Network Layer]
        API -- "HTTP (JSON) + JWT" --> Express[Express.js Server]
    end

    subgraph Server [Node/Express Backend]
        Express --> serverJS[server.js]
        serverJS --> RateLimiter[rateLimiter.js Middleware]
        serverJS --> AuthMiddleware[authMiddleware.js - protect]
        serverJS --> Routes[Routes: authRoutes, scoreRoutes]
        Routes --> Controllers[Controllers: authController, scoreController]
        Controllers --> UserSchema[User.js Mongoose Model]
    end

    subgraph Database [Storage & External Services]
        UserSchema --> MongoDB[MongoDB Atlas]
        Controllers -- "Token Verification" --> GoogleOAuth[Google Identity Services]
    end
```

